PrerequisitesPython 3.10 or 3.11 (64-bit) is recommended.FFmpeg & FFprobe
: Download FFmpeg from gyan.dev or install it via winget (winget install Gyan.FFmpeg). 
: Ensure ffmpeg.exe and ffprobe.exe are added to your system's PATH.  Real-ESRGAN Binary (Optional)
: Place realesrgan-ncnn-vulkan.exe in the application root directory if you plan to use AI 4K upscaling.

Step 1: Set Up a Virtual EnvironmentOpen PowerShell or Command Prompt inside the Media Player folder:PowerShellpython -m venv venv
.\venv\Scripts\activate

Step 2: Install Python DependenciesInstall the core GUI library and feature packages:PowerShell# Core GUI Framework
pip install PyQt6

# AI Subtitle Engine & Cryptographic Vault
pip install faster-whisper numpy cryptography

# Networking, Streaming & Integrations
pip install yt-dlp pypresence pychromecast zeroconf

# Hardware Monitoring
pip install nvidia-ml-py
(Note: In source code, the application specifically prompts for cryptography, yt-dlp, and pychromecast zeroconf when missing).  

For optional features like voice control and AI stem isolation, install:PowerShell# Voice Control (Microphone Listener)
pip install SpeechRecognition pyaudio

# Stem Separation (Demucs AI)
pip install torch demucs
(The app prompts to install SpeechRecognition pyaudio for voice control and notes that torch and demucs are required for stem separation).  

Step 3: requirements.txt (Alternative Quick Setup)You can also save the following list into a requirements.txt file in your app directory:PlaintextPyQt6
faster-whisper
numpy
cryptography
yt-dlp
pypresence
pychromecast
zeroconf
nvidia-ml-py
SpeechRecognition
pyaudio
torch
demucs

Then install all packages simultaneously:PowerShellpip install -r requirements.txt

Step 4: Launch the ApplicationRun the main Python script:PowerShellpython OmniPlayer_Pro_Classic29.py
To run with GPU acceleration for Whisper AI, ensure the NVIDIA CUDA/cuDNN DLLs (cublas64_*.dll, cudnn_*.dll) remain in your script directory or inside your Python site-packages nvidia folder, as the script automatically scans these directories at startup.  You can pass a media file directly via the command line on launch
: PowerShellpython OmniPlayer_Pro_Classic29.py "C:\path\to\your_video.mp4"
